          "domain": "information-and-ideas",
          "skill": "inferences",
          "passage": "Historian Crystal N. Feimster of Yale, in her work on post-Reconstruction lynching, contends that earlier accounts of the era treated the violence as a story driven mainly by men and assigned women a symbolic role on either side: the imperiled white woman invoked to justify mob killings, the bereaved Black woman cast as a figure of grief. Feimster, drawing on club records, courtroom testimony, and the periodical press, documents that Black women organized sustained anti-lynching campaigns and that some white women publicly defended lynch mobs in print and in political organizations. She therefore argues that an analysis attending only to the male protagonists of these conflicts ______",
