          "passage": "In her work along the Jurassic cliffs of Lyme Regis in the early nineteenth century, the fossil collector Mary Anning recovered articulated ichthyosaur and plesiosaur skeletons whose anatomy challenged then-prevailing ideas about the antiquity and diversity of marine reptiles. ______ her contemporary Gideon Mantell, working the chalk and Wealden beds of Sussex, was assembling vertebrate remains that pointed toward an unfamiliar group of large terrestrial reptiles he eventually named Iguanodon.",
