          "domain": "expression-of-ideas",
          "skill": "transitions",
          "passage": "Through the 1950s, most epigraphers working on the Maya glyphic record at Piedras Negras treated the carved dates on the site's stelae as exclusively ritual or calendrical, on the assumption that Classic Maya inscriptions did not record the deeds of named historical individuals. In her 1960 paper for the Peabody Museum, the archaeologist Tatiana Proskouriakoff argued instead that the statistical intervals between the dates on each monument cluster matched human lifespans too closely to be ritual coincidence and were better read as the birth and accession years of named rulers. ______ historians of the Maya treat the figures on those monuments as kings and queens whose reigns can be dated to the year, and the surrounding glyphs as a documentary record of the dynasties that ruled the lowland city-states.",
