          "skill": "words-in-context",
          "passage": "When physicist Lise Meitner read Otto Hahn's December 1938 report that bombarding uranium with neutrons left a faint chemical signature of barium, the result was unexpected enough that most of her colleagues set it aside as a likely contamination. Meitner, in correspondence with her nephew Otto Frisch, instead ____ the finding by treating the uranium nucleus as a charged liquid drop that, jostled by the incoming neutron, could divide into two smaller drops, releasing the energy that the mass difference between parent and products implied.",
