          "skill": "words-in-context",
          "passage": "Before 1957, most physicists treated the idea that the laws of physics are indifferent to a left-right reflection — the symmetry called parity — as a settled feature of every fundamental interaction. The cobalt-60 beta-decay experiment that the experimental physicist Chien-Shiung Wu and her collaborators carried out at the National Bureau of Standards that year ____ that confidence: by recording an angular distribution of emitted electrons that was markedly asymmetric along the axis of nuclear polarization, the experiment showed that the weak force did not respect the symmetry physicists had taken for granted.",
