          "skill": "inferences",
          "passage": "In South to America (2022), Imani Perry of Harvard examines the relation between the American South and the rest of the country. Perry presents two observations she takes to be characteristic of the region. First, arrangements first worked out in the South — concerning labor organization, citizenship, and racial hierarchy — were not contained there but were absorbed into national institutions and continue to organize life across the country. Second, conflicts and crises that observers commonly describe as national in scope tend, on closer examination, to follow patterns that were rehearsed in Southern settings before they became national. Perry's account therefore implies that a study of contemporary American national life that begins by setting the South aside as a regional curiosity ______",
