          "skill": "command-of-evidence-textual",
          "passage": "In Native American DNA: Tribal Belonging and the False Promise of Genetic Science (2013), the anthropologist Kim TallBear, herself an enrolled member of the Sisseton-Wahpeton Oyate, examines the consumer DNA-ancestry tests that promise to confirm a customer's connection to a particular tribal nation. TallBear's argument is that those tests cannot do what they advertise — not because their molecular biology is unreliable but because tribal citizenship in the United States is not a genetic category to begin with. Tribal belonging, she contends, is constituted by political and kinship relations — formal enrollment, lineage records, reciprocal community ties — that no DNA marker measures, so a test result can identify the relative frequency of variants in reference populations without telling anyone whether they are or are not part of a particular nation.",
